cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "authorecon: bibliographic reconciliation and submission hygiene"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vincent
    family-names: Gonzalez
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3640-014X"
    email: vincegonzalez@me.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/vince-gonzalez/apriori"
abstract: >-
  Five commands for the record a research programme leaves behind.
  `authorecon-discover` takes any ORCID and reconciles what the author claims
  against what OpenAlex indexes and what Wikidata holds, using sources that need
  no key, so it can be asked about anyone. The gates run before work leaves your
  hands: `submission-scrub` refuses to let a manuscript reach an editor with
  agent artifacts still in the source; `slop-scan` looks for the structural
  habits that read as machine-written, which a word list cannot find;
  `software-inventory` reports which repositories are in a state anyone could
  cite; `zenodo-precheck` refuses to deposit what is already deposited, by
  comparing attached files rather than titles.

  Standard library only, no dependencies.

keywords:
  - bibliographic reconciliation
  - research software
  - ORCID
  - Zenodo
  - Wikidata
  - OpenAlex
  - submission hygiene
  - research metadata
